      "side": 1,
      "message": "`assertQuery` would inflate the number of queries because it performs additional changes queries for formatting the output.\n\nAlso, just limit to 2 elements, so that you can avoid creating additional changes. With a limit of 2 you can simulate Gerrit trying to make extra queries to fill the results up to its limit.\n\n```suggestion\n    List\u003cChangeInfo\u003e queryResult \u003d newQuery(\"status:new\").withLimit(2).get();\n    assertThat(queryResult).hasSize(1);\n    assertThat(queryResult.get(0).changeId)\n              .isEqualTo(visibleChange2.getKey().get());\n```",
